From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:51:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Set up the ACPI I/O space in the
 bootblock

With vboot in the bootblock (HASWELL_VBOOT_IN_BOOTBLOCK), verstage asks
platform_is_resuming() whether this is an S3 resume, which reads PM1_STS
and PM1_CNT through PMBASE. romstage programs PMBASE and ACPI_EN only
later, in early_pch_init(), so verstage read I/O 0 and 4 instead: the
legacy DMA controller. A cold boot can then look like an S3 resume, and
vboot keeps the slot of the last boot without consuming the tries: a new
slot that an update asked to try is never booted.

Seen on a ThinkPad W541 after an A/B update: nvdata asked for slot B
with two tries, and vboot's work buffer of the next cold boot had
VB2_CONTEXT_S3_RESUME set and no VB2_SD_STATUS_CHOSE_SLOT, so slot A
booted and nvdata was left as it was.

Program PMBASE and enable the ACPI I/O space in the bootblock, as
romstage does again later.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/bootblock.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/bootblock.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/bootblock.c
index d7e719f1c..c11950553 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/bootblock.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/bootblock.c
@@ -39,9 +39,23 @@ static void set_spi_speed(void)
 	RCBA8(SPIBAR_SSFC + 2) = ssfc;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The ACPI I/O space, which romstage sets up again. With vboot in the
+ * bootblock, verstage tells an S3 resume from PM1_STS and PM1_CNT
+ * (platform_is_resuming()): with PMBASE still at its reset value it read the
+ * legacy DMA controller at I/O 0 instead, and could take a cold boot for a
+ * resume, which keeps the slot of the last boot and ignores a slot to try.
+ */
+static void enable_acpi_io(void)
+{
+	pci_write_config32(PCH_LPC_DEV, PMBASE, DEFAULT_PMBASE | 1);
+	pci_write_config8(PCH_LPC_DEV, ACPI_CNTL, ACPI_EN);
+}
+
 void bootblock_early_southbridge_init(void)
 {
 	map_rcba();
+	enable_acpi_io();
 	enable_spi_prefetching_and_caching();
 	enable_port80_on_lpc();
 	set_spi_speed();
